From 621c0821513976dcf1c929c8c8f90356b8795156 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: winsznx <timjosh507@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 11:58:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ec-core: market-scoped fill queries

A binary pool is recycled across successive markets, so one pool address
carries the tape of every market that has ever run on it. The SDK's own
FillRow.market docs say to group by that id and never by pool alone, but
FillsOptions has no market field: getFills(pool, { limit }) applies the
limit to the pool's tape and leaves the caller to filter what survives.

Measured on testnet on 2026-08-28, one 50-row page from pool
0xc09e4a5bdee2899962727125fb5eaeb896798e46 spanned thirteen market
generations, six of them belonging to the market being asked about. At a
smaller page size rows go missing outright: at limit 5 on another recycled
pool, market 48468 returned 4 of its 5 fills. The page size a caller needs
is not a property of the market, it is how many fills the pool has recorded
since that market's oldest fill, and that grows every time the pool is
reused. No fixed limit stays correct and a truncated tape is
indistinguishable from a short one.

market_id is already filterable (FillQueryFields selects it, Fill_bool_exp
accepts it), so these helpers push it into the where clause and the limit
means "rows in this market". Reported upstream against
@somnia-chain/markets-sdk; this gives kit users a correct path meanwhile.

Adds getMarketFills, getMarketUserFills and getAllMarketFills to ec-core,
plus gotcha 17 documenting the measurement.
