+
+### 17. Fills are keyed on a RECYCLED pool address, so `getFills` mixes markets
+
+**Symptom:** a market's trade tape has fills that never happened in it, or is short by
+an amount you cannot explain — and markout, per-market PnL and fill-rate stats are
+quietly wrong.
+
+**Cause:** a binary pool is reused by successive markets, so one pool address carries
+the tape of every market that has ever run on it. The SDK's own `FillRow.market` docs
+say to "group and label by this, never by `pool` alone" — but `FillsOptions` has no
+market field, so `getFills(pool, { limit })` applies the limit to the POOL's tape and
+leaves you to filter client-side, after rows have already been dropped.
+
+Measured on testnet, 2026-08-28: one 50-row page from pool
+`0xc09e4a5bdee2899962727125fb5eaeb896798e46` spanned **thirteen market generations**,
+of which six rows belonged to the market being asked about. The page size you need is
+not a property of the market — it is however many fills the pool has recorded since
+that market's oldest fill, which grows every time the pool is reused. No fixed `limit`
+stays correct, and a truncated tape looks exactly like a short one.
+
+**Fix:** scope by `marketId` server-side. `ec-core` does this:
+
+```ts
+import { getMarketFills, getMarketUserFills, getAllMarketFills } from "@dreamdex-bot-kit/ec-core";
+
+// The last 50 fills IN THIS MARKET — the limit means what you expect.
+const tape = await getMarketFills(market.info.marketId, { limit: 50 }, cfg.indexerUrl);
+
+// Your own fills in one market, as maker or taker.
+const mine = await getMarketUserFills(account, market.info.marketId, { limit: 200 }, cfg.indexerUrl);
+```
+
+Reported upstream against `@somnia-chain/markets-sdk`; these helpers exist so kit users
+have a correct path meanwhile.
